WEBVTT

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:31.630
Set up!

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:32.630
Draw!

00:00:33.220 --> 00:00:36.200
She sends Garon, the Boatman 
of Six Coins to the graveyard!

00:00:37.670 --> 00:00:39.760
Then she plays Cerberus 
The Steel Sword of Fangs!

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:42.020
Approach with Flame Emperor!

00:00:43.780 --> 00:00:46.270
I-I'll use an event!

00:00:46.840 --> 00:00:48.750
Symphony of the Sirens!

00:00:48.750 --> 00:00:52.530
I cancel your approach and make 
you discard a random card.

00:00:53.140 --> 00:00:54.780
I don't know about that.

00:00:54.780 --> 00:00:56.280
This ends it!

00:00:56.960 --> 00:00:58.280
Red dragoon!

00:00:58.280 --> 00:01:00.030
She approaches with this.

00:01:00.920 --> 00:01:03.040
But I don't have any characters left.

00:01:03.620 --> 00:01:07.240
This is your... dead end!

00:01:07.240 --> 00:01:09.540
Approach with Cerberus.

00:01:13.340 --> 00:01:15.300
Let's play Precious Memories again sometime.

00:01:15.940 --> 00:01:19.750
Koyori-chan, will you be my friend?

00:01:20.210 --> 00:01:22.310
After what I did to you?

00:01:31.160 --> 00:01:33.100
I wasn't thinking when I did it.

00:01:36.320 --> 00:01:38.820
That dead end was cool.

00:01:52.770 --> 00:01:54.340
Where did you go?

00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:48.740
I feel out of place here, don't you?

00:03:51.990 --> 00:03:53.260
Welcome!

00:03:54.560 --> 00:03:55.670
Hello.

00:03:55.670 --> 00:03:59.260
Thanks for inviting us somewhere so pretty.

00:03:59.260 --> 00:04:00.590
It's fine.

00:04:00.590 --> 00:04:02.940
This is a showroom for 
a next-generation store,

00:04:02.940 --> 00:04:05.010
so we need to see how 
regular people react, too.

00:04:05.010 --> 00:04:08.010
A student I happen to know 
is more than welcome here.

00:04:08.360 --> 00:04:10.340
This place is amazing, huh?

00:04:10.840 --> 00:04:12.810
Isn't it?

00:04:12.810 --> 00:04:15.400
We spared no expense to make this showroom!

00:04:15.400 --> 00:04:19.100
We couldn't actually make a store like this.

00:04:19.100 --> 00:04:21.200
We can't?

00:04:21.200 --> 00:04:23.150
I was looking forward to it.

00:04:23.420 --> 00:04:26.630
I'm surprised that you're surprised.

00:04:27.490 --> 00:04:29.160
Did you order already?

00:04:29.480 --> 00:04:30.390
Just now...

00:04:31.170 --> 00:04:32.160
It comes out from here?

00:04:33.080 --> 00:04:35.670
The concept is that it's mostly automated.

00:04:35.670 --> 00:04:38.940
You just order with the touch panel 
and it comes out on its own.

00:04:38.940 --> 00:04:41.920
What route did it take to get here?

00:04:42.390 --> 00:04:45.400
You need to control it so it doesn't vibrate.

00:04:45.400 --> 00:04:46.680
How fast does it go? 
What type of motor is it?

00:04:46.980 --> 00:04:51.740
When did they start making it, that it came out so soon after we ordered?

00:04:52.150 --> 00:04:53.980
If they did the cooking the normal way,

00:04:52.150 --> 00:04:53.980
Young man? Young man?

00:04:53.980 --> 00:04:55.190
Tazuna-kun...

00:04:53.980 --> 00:04:57.810
to keep things balanced when it's being 
transported, the conveyor belt...

00:04:58.770 --> 00:05:01.660
He's so good at focusing.

00:05:01.660 --> 00:05:03.650
Is that what beat us?

00:05:03.930 --> 00:05:05.740
S-Sorry.

00:05:05.740 --> 00:05:08.690
I couldn't get things to mesh in my head.

00:05:08.690 --> 00:05:10.160
Sorry, Koyori.

00:05:10.660 --> 00:05:12.660
Have some rice too.

00:05:13.200 --> 00:05:14.910
This place really is amazing though.

00:05:15.210 --> 00:05:18.740
Hayate-san, I know this might 
not be possible, but...

00:05:19.270 --> 00:05:20.920
Can I see what's inside?

00:05:21.280 --> 00:05:23.680
No, I don't think that's possible...

00:05:23.680 --> 00:05:25.900
But I know how you feel.

00:05:25.900 --> 00:05:28.220
It's so cool the way it comes automatically.

00:05:28.220 --> 00:05:31.430
You could use this system 
for a lot of things, huh?

00:05:31.740 --> 00:05:34.520
You're so ambitious.

00:05:34.520 --> 00:05:36.620
You're such a boy.

00:05:38.590 --> 00:05:40.640
Man, I can't stop thinking about it...

00:05:40.640 --> 00:05:44.410
Hey, Tazuna-kun, why don't 
we go for a bike ride?

00:05:44.410 --> 00:05:45.440
What's wrong?

00:05:44.840 --> 00:05:45.950
That sounds great!

00:05:45.950 --> 00:05:49.470
I've never gone that far.

00:05:49.470 --> 00:05:53.230
I just don't get very many 
chances to exercise...

00:05:54.140 --> 00:05:55.980
Cantilever breaks are so cool.

00:05:55.980 --> 00:05:58.140
That's pretty hardcore!

00:05:55.980 --> 00:05:59.030
You want to cook for him, right?

00:06:01.160 --> 00:06:04.590
I hope I can teach you right,

00:06:04.590 --> 00:06:06.700
but I've got my work,

00:06:06.700 --> 00:06:09.590
and I can't come over to your house.

00:06:10.320 --> 00:06:11.770
Do you have a phone?

00:06:13.100 --> 00:06:15.740
Then borrow Tazuna-kun's...

00:06:15.740 --> 00:06:17.460
Do you know how to use one?

00:06:18.810 --> 00:06:22.420
So you'd look at something 
like this, and then...

00:06:23.280 --> 00:06:25.700
You'd just have to practice.

00:06:26.110 --> 00:06:28.720
I had a really hard time at first, too.

00:06:28.720 --> 00:06:29.860
The side dishes at the supermarket...

00:06:30.170 --> 00:06:32.480
Oh, the parfait's melting.

00:06:32.120 --> 00:06:39.000
...and so I've got nothing to do on the 
way there, so I listen to the radio...

00:06:32.480 --> 00:06:33.870
Eat it first.

00:06:36.660 --> 00:06:38.460
Youth!

00:06:39.250 --> 00:06:40.270
What's wrong?

00:06:40.270 --> 00:06:45.870
The pure things we lost as we grew up...

00:06:45.870 --> 00:06:47.870
I was feeling them.

00:06:47.870 --> 00:06:51.240
You don't look like you've grown up though.

00:06:51.240 --> 00:06:53.230
So anyway, my car,

00:06:53.230 --> 00:06:55.740
I've modified the speakers!

00:06:55.740 --> 00:06:56.810
That's great!

00:06:56.810 --> 00:06:58.310
Let me see them some time!

00:06:59.080 --> 00:07:01.160
These boys...

00:07:02.160 --> 00:07:04.570
That was amazing.

00:07:04.570 --> 00:07:09.740
I don't know if the Centeotl Group 
could make all that stuff itself.

00:07:09.740 --> 00:07:11.740
Those quiet motors...

00:07:12.090 --> 00:07:13.740
Where were they made?

00:07:14.060 --> 00:07:16.370
Japan? Overseas?

00:07:16.820 --> 00:07:17.900
Or maybe...

00:07:18.370 --> 00:07:19.960
I really want to see how they work.

00:07:28.770 --> 00:07:29.630
Koyori?!

00:07:31.120 --> 00:07:32.490
Oh, no!

00:07:32.490 --> 00:07:34.140
Koyori doesn't have a cell phone.

00:07:34.760 --> 00:07:37.580
Why didn't I give her one?

00:07:39.090 --> 00:07:42.140
If I thought about it at all,
 I would've known...

00:07:42.600 --> 00:07:43.900
Of all the things that could happen...

00:08:26.160 --> 00:08:27.380
Koyori-chan?

00:08:36.660 --> 00:08:39.130
N-No...

00:08:39.760 --> 00:08:42.250
Sis, you actually look 
more suspicious that way.

00:08:45.430 --> 00:08:47.000
It's no good! I can't find her!

00:08:47.340 --> 00:08:49.500
<i>I'm sorry, I wasn't thinking either!</i>

00:08:51.310 --> 00:08:54.730
<i>We should've at least thought</i>

00:08:54.730 --> 00:08:58.090
<i>about using GPS to locate her or something...</i>

00:08:58.640 --> 00:09:00.370
<i>But I...</i>

00:09:00.370 --> 00:09:03.110
<i>No, I can't be getting excited, huh?</i>

00:09:03.750 --> 00:09:06.460
Is Koyori okay?

00:09:06.980 --> 00:09:09.270
She hasn't disappeared already...

00:09:09.920 --> 00:09:14.150
If she's not inside the Ziggurat, 
I can guarantee you two hours.

00:09:14.580 --> 00:09:15.800
Two hours?

00:09:15.800 --> 00:09:16.970
<i>You're still okay.</i>

00:09:16.970 --> 00:09:18.160
<i>I'm sure of that.</i>

00:09:18.850 --> 00:09:20.300
I'll find her.

00:09:20.300 --> 00:09:21.900
I promise I'll find her.

00:09:21.900 --> 00:09:23.100
I won't...

00:09:23.660 --> 00:09:25.160
<i>Tazuna-kun?</i>

00:09:29.170 --> 00:09:30.330
Koyori?

00:09:30.330 --> 00:09:32.150
<i>What's wrong, Tazuna-kun?</i>

00:09:32.150 --> 00:09:34.460
Sorry, I'm hanging up.

00:09:41.010 --> 00:09:41.930
She's not here.

00:09:42.610 --> 00:09:44.520
Did I pass her?

00:09:44.520 --> 00:09:46.040
Looking for something?

00:09:57.240 --> 00:10:00.370
Did a girl come this way?

00:10:01.490 --> 00:10:03.610
A girl?

00:10:04.710 --> 00:10:07.120
Do you know how many girls 
there are in this world?

00:10:07.620 --> 00:10:09.850
You're right...

00:10:09.850 --> 00:10:10.630
Bye.

00:10:10.630 --> 00:10:11.630
Wait.

00:10:12.160 --> 00:10:15.130
Do you need something?

00:10:21.200 --> 00:10:23.890
How's school lately?

00:10:26.740 --> 00:10:29.390
Does he still like shumai?

00:10:31.360 --> 00:10:35.240
No, I just couldn't think of what to say.

00:10:35.240 --> 00:10:36.400
<i>He's a poor talker.</i>

00:10:37.900 --> 00:10:39.400
Is Makihara doing okay?

00:10:43.350 --> 00:10:48.740
We will now begin the Precious Memories 
Osaka Tournament, sponsored by Card Lab!

00:10:45.410 --> 00:10:49.040
<b>Osaka Tournament</b>

00:10:49.320 --> 00:10:50.910
That's a trap!

00:10:50.910 --> 00:10:52.420
This is my real one!

00:10:52.420 --> 00:10:54.040
Four sets! That's all!

00:10:54.040 --> 00:10:55.420
Yes!

00:10:56.150 --> 00:10:57.920
I'm back, Koyori-chan.

00:10:57.920 --> 00:11:01.080
I'm sorry, I can't get a hold of Tazuna-kun.

00:11:01.080 --> 00:11:02.680
I'll call him later.

00:11:06.500 --> 00:11:07.310
Masaru...?

00:11:08.230 --> 00:11:09.720
He's in the finals, right?

00:11:10.620 --> 00:11:11.910
It's my turn.

00:11:12.550 --> 00:11:15.320
I use the text for Deathcase Volcano!

00:11:15.800 --> 00:11:20.200
I put two cards in my point storage 
area and play my discarded card!

00:11:21.640 --> 00:11:22.920
No way...

00:11:22.920 --> 00:11:25.580
One more point and you lose. Are you insane?

00:11:25.580 --> 00:11:27.610
I'm totally sane.

00:11:27.610 --> 00:11:29.580
Why would I need to hesitate?

00:11:29.580 --> 00:11:34.360
You're going to be burned by Crimson 
Hellfire and lose this turn.

00:11:35.090 --> 00:11:36.240
Is that it?

00:11:36.240 --> 00:11:37.580
Is he going to use it?

00:11:38.210 --> 00:11:39.590
He sure is!

00:11:39.950 --> 00:11:43.840
I play Flame Emperor, the Dragon of 
Crimson Heavens, from my discarded cards!

00:11:43.840 --> 00:11:44.910
That's it!

00:11:44.910 --> 00:11:47.220
The ace of the Dead End Emperor!

00:11:47.220 --> 00:11:50.650
You couldn't do that unless you 
were sure you were going to win!

00:11:50.650 --> 00:11:52.230
Way to go, Emperor!

00:11:52.230 --> 00:11:54.460
You're so cool, Masaru!

00:11:54.460 --> 00:11:56.730
That's the Dead End Emperor for you!

00:11:57.300 --> 00:12:00.070
I love the Dead End!

00:12:02.880 --> 00:12:04.490
The Emperor.

00:12:05.030 --> 00:12:07.000
Rule. Authority.

00:12:07.480 --> 00:12:10.380
In other words, 
this is the zone of the Emperor.

00:12:10.380 --> 00:12:13.000
Emperor's big sis is always so loud...

00:12:13.400 --> 00:12:16.250
This is your dead end!

00:12:16.630 --> 00:12:19.760
Approach with Flame Emperor!

00:12:20.920 --> 00:12:24.600
The winner is the Demon Emperor of 
the Apocalypse, the Dead End Emperor,

00:12:24.600 --> 00:12:26.040
Houjou Masaru!

00:12:28.090 --> 00:12:29.480
Wow!

00:12:28.560 --> 00:12:30.000
He got burnt to a crisp!

00:12:29.480 --> 00:12:31.800
That was an amazing dead end, Masaru!

00:12:31.800 --> 00:12:33.770
That's my emperor!

00:12:39.510 --> 00:12:41.530
I think that was a good match.

00:12:42.050 --> 00:12:43.560
The emperor...

00:12:46.130 --> 00:12:48.410
You've got a good sister, huh?

00:12:48.410 --> 00:12:50.590
Masaru, you did it!

00:12:50.590 --> 00:12:52.040
Isn't that great?

00:12:52.040 --> 00:12:53.470
Four wins in a row!

00:12:53.470 --> 00:12:55.040
Next it's on to the nationals...

00:12:55.480 --> 00:12:56.560
Sheesh.

00:12:56.560 --> 00:12:57.800
We're going home.

00:12:58.530 --> 00:12:59.540
I'm so embarrassed.

00:13:01.570 --> 00:13:03.050
Masaru...

00:13:09.190 --> 00:13:11.010
Our plans got messed up.

00:13:16.890 --> 00:13:18.520
You interested in my cards?

00:13:23.330 --> 00:13:25.030
Want to try some Precious Memories?

00:13:25.810 --> 00:13:29.300
You know Makihara-sensei?

00:13:29.300 --> 00:13:31.560
Do I know him?

00:13:32.650 --> 00:13:35.240
I guess you could say I know him.

00:13:36.000 --> 00:13:37.790
You could say I don't know him...

00:13:39.730 --> 00:13:41.560
But no, I know.

00:13:41.560 --> 00:13:43.520
<i>He really is bad at talking.</i>

00:13:43.520 --> 00:13:46.490
Um, you don't have to try to act cool.

00:13:46.490 --> 00:13:48.120
I'm in a hurry.

00:13:50.950 --> 00:13:52.490
I'll ask you instead.

00:13:52.490 --> 00:13:54.620
Do you know him?

00:13:54.620 --> 00:13:57.310
Listen, you really don't need 
to try and impress me...

00:13:58.240 --> 00:14:01.060
Makihara was originally a Hand Shaker.

00:14:03.110 --> 00:14:05.610
I figured he hadn't told you.

00:14:05.610 --> 00:14:07.340
Who are you...?

00:14:08.400 --> 00:14:10.070
Why are you fighting?

00:14:11.970 --> 00:14:13.080
I...

00:14:15.020 --> 00:14:17.750
Destroying the wishes of others.

00:14:18.840 --> 00:14:21.500
That's what you're doing.

00:14:25.670 --> 00:14:29.290
You haven't even discovered the 
god you're supposed to find.

00:14:29.290 --> 00:14:31.660
No, you don't even have a wish.

00:14:33.620 --> 00:14:34.680
Who...

00:14:35.920 --> 00:14:37.510
Who are you?

00:14:38.880 --> 00:14:41.630
Who am I, huh?

00:14:41.630 --> 00:14:42.790
I said...

00:14:43.190 --> 00:14:45.440
Are you just going to do 
what Makihara tells you?

00:14:48.020 --> 00:14:49.200
I'm...

00:14:49.200 --> 00:14:51.700
You're fighting to keep Koyori alive.

00:14:54.040 --> 00:14:56.700
Koyori reminds you of your own sister...

00:14:59.000 --> 00:15:00.460
N-No...

00:15:00.460 --> 00:15:05.900
That isn't Takatsuki Musubu, your sister.

00:15:05.900 --> 00:15:09.470
Are you still going to do 
what Makihara tells you?

00:15:10.170 --> 00:15:11.980
It feels like you've gotten used to it now,

00:15:11.980 --> 00:15:13.470
so I'll get serious.

00:15:17.760 --> 00:15:19.720
Approach with Flame Emperor!

00:15:19.720 --> 00:15:22.640
This is your dead end!

00:15:22.640 --> 00:15:24.230
I win!

00:15:29.360 --> 00:15:31.230
The reverse moon.

00:15:31.230 --> 00:15:34.060
Bewitchment. Hidden danger.

00:15:34.490 --> 00:15:37.240
I can't believe Koyori-chan is so good.

00:15:37.810 --> 00:15:40.920
I'm not a match for her yet.

00:15:40.920 --> 00:15:43.300
You're not even that good at the game.

00:15:44.500 --> 00:15:46.040
Masaru...

00:15:46.040 --> 00:15:49.010
But even if I lent you my cards,

00:15:49.480 --> 00:15:51.260
I can't believe I'm having to fight so hard

00:15:51.260 --> 00:15:53.400
against someone who just 
started playing today.

00:15:53.830 --> 00:15:56.000
You learn fast...

00:15:56.390 --> 00:15:57.890
Yeah, it was fun.

00:15:58.900 --> 00:16:00.390
One more game?

00:16:01.090 --> 00:16:02.630
As many as you want.

00:16:07.240 --> 00:16:08.310
What?

00:16:09.300 --> 00:16:11.610
I have to call Tazuna-kun!

00:16:11.610 --> 00:16:13.640
I'm not a kid.

00:16:13.640 --> 00:16:16.180
You don't have to follow me here.

00:16:13.640 --> 00:16:16.180
Excuse me, Koyori-chan...

00:16:22.500 --> 00:16:24.550
I don't hate her or anything.

00:16:24.550 --> 00:16:26.820
She's just a bit of a nuisance.

00:16:28.270 --> 00:16:29.690
Let's just do this.

00:16:29.690 --> 00:16:31.700
You can go first.

00:16:34.020 --> 00:16:35.140
I...

00:16:36.160 --> 00:16:37.420
Koyori...

00:16:39.890 --> 00:16:41.960
Shouldn't you answer that?

00:16:44.040 --> 00:16:46.280
President Lily? I'm...

00:16:47.330 --> 00:16:48.650
Koyori's with you?

00:16:48.960 --> 00:16:50.900
I'll head there now. Thanks!

00:16:58.910 --> 00:17:03.260
You who will overcome many 
battles and trials...

00:17:03.260 --> 00:17:05.420
You who received the Revelation.

00:17:05.420 --> 00:17:08.920
You who would challenge me.

00:17:08.920 --> 00:17:11.170
Yes, you, the Hand Shaker...

00:17:14.510 --> 00:17:17.510
Makihara, that's a sin.

00:17:18.020 --> 00:17:19.500
Isn't that great?

00:17:19.500 --> 00:17:21.770
Tazuna-kun says he'll be here soon.

00:17:24.390 --> 00:17:25.520
No way!

00:17:27.440 --> 00:17:29.500
Reverse Temperance!

00:17:29.500 --> 00:17:30.730
Waste?

00:17:30.730 --> 00:17:33.530
I forgot I used the money for lunch...

00:17:33.820 --> 00:17:36.570
I was planning to withdraw some money!

00:17:39.680 --> 00:17:41.280
I'll pay.

00:17:41.280 --> 00:17:45.540
Oh no, Masaru, your sister can...

00:17:45.870 --> 00:17:48.490
You can always count on your big sister...

00:17:48.490 --> 00:17:50.860
Masaru...

00:17:51.540 --> 00:17:56.220
You used too much money because 
you bought me lunch, right?

00:17:59.300 --> 00:18:01.550
Thank you, Masaru!

00:18:09.090 --> 00:18:12.170
My dignity as an older sister is ruined...

00:18:14.320 --> 00:18:17.380
I wish I had my act together more,

00:18:18.260 --> 00:18:22.340
but I always look so stupid 
when I'm around Masaru.

00:18:23.280 --> 00:18:26.580
Maybe I'm letting him spoil me, 
even though he's my little brother.

00:18:27.200 --> 00:18:30.410
But Masaru's a really smart kid.

00:18:30.410 --> 00:18:32.160
His card's the Emperor, you know?

00:18:32.160 --> 00:18:34.590
He's smart, and he thinks on his feet.

00:18:34.590 --> 00:18:37.880
Lately he's been getting stronger,

00:18:37.880 --> 00:18:40.160
and he's getting taller...

00:18:40.160 --> 00:18:43.140
When I peeked in the bath a 
while ago, I was a little...

00:18:44.100 --> 00:18:47.930
Koyori-chan, you're really good 
friends with Tazuna-kun, right?

00:18:48.470 --> 00:18:52.110
Um, well... um...

00:18:52.460 --> 00:18:54.980
Oh, never mind! It's nothing!

00:18:55.860 --> 00:18:58.340
But... um...

00:19:00.860 --> 00:19:04.220
Is it weird to be in love

00:19:05.220 --> 00:19:06.870
with your little brother?

00:19:12.080 --> 00:19:13.130
Koyori!

00:19:19.190 --> 00:19:20.250
Koyori!

00:19:42.720 --> 00:19:44.000
I'm sorry.

00:19:44.000 --> 00:19:45.660
Are you okay? Does it hurt?

00:19:52.390 --> 00:19:55.130
President Lily, thank you.
 You were a big help.

00:19:55.130 --> 00:19:56.920
No, I'm really glad...

00:20:04.290 --> 00:20:06.680
Okay, first let's hit up an ATM.

00:20:32.000 --> 00:20:32.980
No way...

00:20:33.490 --> 00:20:35.770
Tazuna-kun's a Hand Shaker...

00:20:35.770 --> 00:20:36.710
Sis...

00:20:37.220 --> 00:20:38.810
President Lily...

00:20:39.990 --> 00:20:40.960
Are we going to fight?

00:20:40.960 --> 00:20:45.240
No... I don't want to fight like this.

00:20:45.240 --> 00:20:46.470
Not with you!

00:20:46.760 --> 00:20:50.070
Then wish for the fight to stop.

00:20:50.640 --> 00:20:52.480
If we both lose our will to fight,

00:20:52.480 --> 00:20:54.480
we'll be kicked out of the Ziggurat.

00:20:55.220 --> 00:20:56.980
<i>That's what Makihara-sensei said.</i>

00:20:56.980 --> 00:20:58.410
Y-Yeah...

00:20:59.270 --> 00:21:01.940
I can't fight Tazuna-kun.

00:21:09.650 --> 00:21:10.820
Why?

00:21:11.940 --> 00:21:14.430
It means you want to fight us, right?

00:21:14.430 --> 00:21:15.460
Masaru?

00:21:15.890 --> 00:21:18.210
Sis, we have to fight.

00:21:19.830 --> 00:21:20.570
Yeah.

00:21:21.240 --> 00:21:22.210
President Lily!

00:21:22.610 --> 00:21:24.220
If you want to fight...

00:21:24.520 --> 00:21:25.470
...then let's start!

00:21:25.940 --> 00:21:26.970
Standby!

00:21:31.970 --> 00:21:35.510
So this is the President's Nimrod...

00:23:11.030 --> 00:23:13.240
<i>I fell in love with you, sadly.</i>

00:23:13.240 --> 00:23:15.720
<i>I can't read the future of these feelings.</i>

00:23:15.720 --> 00:23:17.850
<i>I fell in love with you, sadly.</i>

00:23:17.850 --> 00:23:20.490
<i>I'll turn my love into burning flames.</i>

00:23:20.490 --> 00:23:23.580
<i>It's too young to call forbidden, 
and too fierce.</i>

00:23:24.150 --> 00:23:26.630
<i>The deck shrinks. The gears spin.</i>

00:23:26.930 --> 00:23:29.670
<i>If I defeat you, my wish will come true.</i>

00:23:29.670 --> 00:23:34.710
<i>Next time on Hand Shakers, 
Episode 6: Emperor of Fortune.</i>

00:23:35.140 --> 00:23:38.730
<i>The last card unleashed is their truth.</i>
